From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bcrypt, crypt32: raw RSA, BCryptGenRandom's RNG pseudo-handle, CertFindChainInStore

- Raw RSA (BCRYPT_PAD_NONE; NCrypt's NCRYPT_NO_PADDING_FLAG) was
  STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED: a whole block is raised to the key's public or
  private exponent modulo its modulus (GnuTLS has no call for it; GMP,
  which GnuTLS's own arithmetic uses, is loaded for the arithmetic). A
  block that is not the key's size, or not below its modulus, is
  STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER; the size is given with no output buffer.
  Wine's bcrypt test no longer marks these as todo.
- BCryptGenRandom takes the RNG pseudo-handle (BCRYPT_RNG_ALG_HANDLE),
  which failed with STATUS_NOT_IMPLEMENTED unless the system generator
  flag was also given; a handle together with
  BCRYPT_USE_SYSTEM_PREFERRED_RNG, or unknown flags, is
  STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER; BCRYPT_RNG_USE_ENTROPY_IN_BUFFER is accepted
  (ignored, as documented). BCryptOpenAlgorithmProvider accepts
  BCRYPT_PROV_DISPATCH and BCRYPT_CAPI_AES_FLAG; a caller's object buffer
  is not needed (no FIXME).
- CertFindChainInStore (a stub that found nothing) finds, for
  CERT_CHAIN_FIND_BY_ISSUER, the chains of the store's certificates that
  have a private key (unless CERT_CHAIN_FIND_BY_ISSUER_NO_KEY_FLAG; the
  key checked against the certificate with ..._COMPARE_KEY_FLAG), are good
  for the usage asked, pass the caller's callback and have one of the
  issuers given in the chain, telling where; each call goes on after the
  previous chain. CERT_CHAIN_FIND_BY_ISSUER_PARA and its flags are added
  to wincrypt.h.

Wine's bcrypt test: the raw RSA todos pass; crypt32 chain: as before.

Gate: test/cryptrest-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/cryptrest-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_RAW_RSA (bcrypt/gnutls.c), SG_MUTANT_NO_FIND_CHAIN
(crypt32/chain.c).
